    <item>
      <title>train ambush: nausicaä</title>
      <link>http://localhost:1313/blog/nausicaa/</link>
      <pubDate>Sat, 11 Jul 2026 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate>
      <guid>http://localhost:1313/blog/nausicaa/</guid>
      <description>&lt;p&gt;During the June heatwave, I took an 8-hour train that was thankfully air-conditioned, on time, and very comfortable—thanks České dráhy! The first half of that fiery, disgusting day had sucked me dry of any hint of energy (for an accurate visual representation, I refer readers to &lt;a href=&#34;https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=HMRcFS35Mv8&#34;&gt;an iconic Indian TV ad from maybe the 2000s&lt;/a&gt;). And there was a huge group of teenagers just in front of me, so I needed to be properly distracted in order to keep the already-twitching crankiness dial under control. So, I scrolled the usual apps for something to watch: something engrossing, but light and not very demanding. Netflix seemed to have a lot of the Miyazaki x Ghibli movies—I&amp;rsquo;m a fan, but I haven&amp;rsquo;t watched them all. I landed on Nausicaä of the Valley of the Wind.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
    </item>
    <item>
      <title></title>
      <link>http://localhost:1313/about/</link>
      <pubDate>Mon, 01 Jan 0001 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate>
      <guid>http://localhost:1313/about/</guid>
      <description>&lt;h6 class=&#34;heading&#34; id=&#34;projects&#34;&gt;&#xA;  projects&#xA;  &lt;a class=&#34;anchor&#34; href=&#34;#projects&#34;&gt;#&lt;/a&gt;&#xA;&lt;/h6&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;In my doctoral project, I am investigating things that look like quotations in spoken language (such as airquotes and enactments) under the supervision of &lt;a href=&#34;https://www.leibniz-zas.de/en/people/details/sauerland-uli/uli-sauerland/&#34;&gt;Uli Sauerland&lt;/a&gt; here at ZAS and &lt;a href=&#34;https://michael-franke.github.io/heimseite/&#34;&gt;Michael Franke&lt;/a&gt; at the University of Tübingen.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;At ZAS, I am part of the &lt;a href=&#34;https://www.leibniz-zas.de/en/research/research-areas/semantics-pragmatics/lmbayes&#34;&gt;LMBayes&lt;/a&gt; project which focuses on developing probabilistic models of meaning.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;I also enjoy puzzling over the &amp;ldquo;depth-charge&amp;rdquo; illusion, which was the topic of my MSc thesis and continues to be a source of delight.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
    </item>
